{:edb/db-before-t 1175 :edb/db-after-t 1176 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534488 50 #inst "2026-10-07T08:18:00.882Z" 13194139534488 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291593 13194139534488 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291600 13194139534488 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291607 13194139534488 true] [17592186060374 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534488 true] [17592186060374 1100 "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2k + 1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis singular." 13194139534488 false] [17592186060374 1100 "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2k+1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." 13194139534488 true] [17592186060374 1145 "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2k+1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2k+1 & k \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}2k+1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3-0)-(2k+1-k)-4(0-3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-(k+1)-4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6-k-1+12 \\\\  & =17-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17-k & =0 \\\\ k & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=17.$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186060381 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534488 true] [17592186060381 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\n- $det(F)=0$\n- $F$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(F)=-2$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186060381 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\n1. $\\det(F) = 0$\n2. $F$ is a singular matrix\n3. $\\det(F) =-2$\n\n$$\nF = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139534488 false] [17592186060381 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-1(24-30)+2(21-24) \\\\  & =0-1\\cdot (-6)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6-6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534488 true] [17592186291593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291594 13194139534488 true] [17592186291593 1089 "q-128478" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534488 true] [17592186291593 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $F$ given below?\n\n- $det(F)=-7$\n- $F$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(F)=-2$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291593 1113 #uuid "af5c321a-ef93-52c0-aab1-818de4211e7b" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291593 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-8|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2-3)-8(-1-5)+3(-3-10) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-8\\cdot (-6)+3\\cdot (-13) \\\\  & =-2+48-39 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(F)=7$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291595 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291596 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291597 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291598 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291599 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1041 "selection" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291599 13194139534488 true] [17592186291594 1110 #uuid "c93f4e79-80f7-52a5-9175-9f28ad8128d1" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291595 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534488 true] [17592186291595 1111 #uuid "e4ca2415-9cc0-55d6-a117-9433092650cf" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291596 1034 "None of the given statements are true" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534488 true] [17592186291596 1111 #uuid "b8bba62d-fe77-5d81-bcef-93aa7bb31ccd" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291597 1034 "I only" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534488 true] [17592186291597 1111 #uuid "298fd41d-0b67-5dd7-a7f4-b00d36ea9393" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291598 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534488 true] [17592186291598 1111 #uuid "80942402-97be-50b4-81e8-4df0f85fbddf" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291599 1034 "II only" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534488 true] [17592186291599 1111 #uuid "e9a9e36b-c45e-5d89-95dc-ea4a477b71b8" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291601 13194139534488 true] [17592186291600 1089 "q-128502" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291600 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534488 true] [17592186291600 1100 "Given that \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand $det(C)=28,$ find the value of $q.$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291600 1113 #uuid "e0915dbf-e532-5db3-bdaa-4adfc7076ccf" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291600 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}q & 5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (q+25)-3\\cdot (-1)+5 \\\\  & =2q+58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $28,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q+58 & =28 \\\\ 2q & =-30 \\\\ q & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291602 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291603 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291604 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291605 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291606 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1041 "selection" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291604 13194139534488 true] [17592186291601 1110 #uuid "7400cdc3-34b8-5532-bf3f-8e25d803e6d1" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291602 1034 "12" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534488 true] [17592186291602 1111 #uuid "7f75060d-2e3e-5e90-9815-cb9194a8788a" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291603 1034 "20" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534488 true] [17592186291603 1111 #uuid "fb0d6a44-8436-5525-8cb9-406699916693" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291604 1034 "-15" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534488 true] [17592186291604 1111 #uuid "68b24bc2-38bc-5cf1-a568-635bf94c79e0" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291605 1034 "-10" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534488 true] [17592186291605 1111 #uuid "7c0e1d50-c0da-51ed-9ef3-211ca52408f1" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291606 1034 "2" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534488 true] [17592186291606 1111 #uuid "c134ccc7-ce69-567f-94f5-e833ae2ba4be" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291607 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291608 13194139534488 true] [17592186291607 1089 "q-130575" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291607 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534488 true] [17592186291607 1100 "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-48$, find all the possible values of $z.$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291607 1113 #uuid "d07c9ad8-9277-516a-802b-f65168b9d077" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291607 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & z \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ z & 1\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ z & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3+z)-(2-{z}^{2})+5(-2-3z) \\\\  & =6+2z-2+{z}^{2}-10-15z \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-13z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-48,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-13z-6 & =-48 \\\\ {z}^{2}-13z+42 & =0 \\\\ z & =\\frac{-(-13)\\pm \\sqrt{{13}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 42}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm \\sqrt{1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm 1}{2} \\\\  & =6,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=6$ and $z=7.$" 13194139534488 true] [17592186291608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291609 13194139534488 true] [17592186291608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291610 13194139534488 true] [17592186291608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291611 13194139534488 true] [1759